{"duration_api_ms":2254736,"stop_reason":"end_turn","session_id":"b5b42b1e-07e1-41c2-94e8-556b69ff0215","total_cost_usd":72.36215200000001,"usage":{"input_tokens":64,"cache_creation_input_tokens":31133,"cache_read_input_tokens":19010529,"output_tokens":18125,"output_tokens_details":{"thinking_tokens":5637},"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":31133,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0},"inference_geo":"not_available","iterations":[{"input_tokens":2,"output_tokens":2874,"cache_read_input_tokens":607705,"cache_creation_input_tokens":1928,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":1928},"type":"message"}],"speed":"standard"},"modelUsage":{"claude-opus-5[1m]":{"inputTokens":672,"outputTokens":159510,"thinkingTokens":53557,"cacheReadInputTokens":125308584,"cacheCreationInputTokens":571675,"webSearchRequests":0,"costUSD":72.36215200000001,"contextWindow":1000000,"maxOutputTokens":64000,"canonicalModel":"claude-opus-5","provider":"firstParty","costBasis":"list"}},"permission_denials":[],"terminal_reason":"completed","fast_mode_state":"off","fast_mode_disabled_reason":"sdk_opt_in_required","subagent_stats":{"spawned":0,"requested":{"background":0,"foreground":0,"unset":0},"started_in_background":0,"max_depth":0,"spawned_by_subagents":0,"completed":0,"failed":0,"killed":{"parent":0,"user":0,"system":0},"refused":{"depth_limit":0,"concurrency_limit":0,"budget":0},"by_type":{}},"is_error":false,"num_turns":32,"subtype":"success","api_error_status":null,"result":"All five are complete and verified.\n\n## Per item (killed-turn vs now)\n\n**A2 — `launchURL` scheme gate** · *killed turn, complete; verified now by reading*\n`lib/utils/page_utils.dart`. `http`/`https` open directly. `file/content/javascript/data/blob/about/filesystem` stay hard-blocked with a toast, not confirmable. Every other scheme (custom app schemes included) now goes through a confirm dialog naming the scheme and the full target before it reaches the OS. Added the `dialog.dart` import.\n\n**A12 — Linux anonymous jar on logout** · *killed turn, complete; verified now by reading*\n`lib/utils/login_utils.dart`. `onLogoutMain` no longer branches per platform: it calls `clearWebCookies()` (which already does the right per-platform delete) then `setAnonymousWebCookie()`, on both. `setAnonymousWebCookie`'s Linux early-return now carries the reason it is a correct no-op: desktop_webview_window exposes no set-cookie API and keeps no jar between windows, and `WebviewPage.openLinux` injects the anonymous `buvid3` from `AnonymousAccount()` at documentStart for every window it opens.\n\n**A30 — block-server matching** · *killed turn, complete; verified now by test*\n`lib/utils/accounts/account_manager/account_mgr.dart` + `lib/pages/sponsor_block/view.dart`. New public `parseBlockServer(String)`: requires `http(s)`, a non-empty host, no userinfo, and refuses the bilibili family by suffix (`bilibili.com/.cn/.tv`, `bilivideo.com/.cn`, `hdslb.com`, `biliimg.com`, `b23.tv`). `_isBlockServer` now matches scheme + host + **port** + path prefix and returns false outright when `parseBlockServer` rejects the saved value — so it cannot degrade into \"matches everything\". The settings dialog calls the same function, so the two cannot diverge.\n\n**A31 — `handler.next` on the retry path** · *killed turn, code written; verified now by test*\n`lib/http/retry_interceptor.dart`. The retry path now ends in `handler.next(error)` for the attempt the caller made. Because each retry re-enters the interceptor on the same `RequestOptions`, a naive `next` everywhere delivered the same failure once per retry level (I measured 3 deliveries with `retryCount=2`); a `finish()` helper keyed on whether `_rt` was already present makes the nested levels reject and only the outermost forward. Measured: 3 adapter calls, **1** delivery to the following interceptor, request still fails. A non-retried POST still reaches it once.\n\n**A37 — refresh coalescing** · *killed turn, base written; completed and verified now*\n`lib/pages/common/common_list_controller.dart` (+3 controllers). A refresh started while one is in flight now attaches to it instead of issuing a second request; `_generation` is untouched, so when a request *is* made the superseded response is still dropped. Added `markRefreshStale()` for the case that made me revert this in batch A — a refresh whose parameters differ must not attach to one answering the old ones. `onReload()` calls it (covers sort/filter/account-switch, which all route through it). **New this turn:** I audited the direct `onRefresh()` call sites and found three keyword-driven paths that bypass `onReload` — `CommonSearchController.onRefresh` (every search page), `DynMentionController.onRefresh`, `SelectTopicController` (which had no override; added one). `LiveAreaDetail.onSelectTag` needs nothing: it early-returns on `isLoading`.\n\n## Diff summary\n\n| File | ± |\n|---|---|\n| `lib/utils/page_utils.dart` | +36 −0 |\n| `lib/utils/login_utils.dart` | +14 −5 |\n| `lib/utils/accounts/account_manager/account_mgr.dart` | +51 −7 |\n| `lib/pages/sponsor_block/view.dart` | +11 −6 |\n| `lib/http/retry_interceptor.dart` | +25 −9 |\n| `lib/pages/common/common_list_controller.dart` | +31 −1 |\n| `lib/pages/common/search/common_search_controller.dart` | +3 −0 |\n| `lib/pages/dynamics_mention/controller.dart` | +3 −0 |\n| `lib/pages/dynamics_select_topic/controller.dart` | +8 −0 |\n\n179 insertions, 29 deletions across 9 files. Three regression tests added under `test/utils/` (gitignored): `retry_interceptor_test.dart`, `refresh_coalescing_test.dart`, `block_server_test.dart`. `dart format` reports no changes on all 57 touched files.\n\n## Uncertainties\n\n- **A2, no context:** `launchURL` needs a `BuildContext` for the confirm, and takes `Get.context`. If that is null (very early startup, or a call from outside the widget tree) a non-http(s) url is now silently dropped rather than opened. All call sites I checked are user-initiated from a live page, so this should not fire, but it is a behaviour change if it does.\n- **A2, our own scheme:** an unrecognised `bilibili://` link inside a web page (one `PiliScheme.routePush` did not match) now prompts before being handed back to the OS. I judged that correct rather than exempting `bilibili`; say if you'd rather it be silent.\n- **A12, Linux:** I could not run Linux. The claim that the anonymous jar is reinstated there rests on reading `WebviewPage.openLinux` (`webview/view.dart:67-78`) — it builds the injection JS from `AnonymousAccount()` for every non-account window. If a future change opens a Linux webview without going through `openLinux`, that window would have an empty jar.\n- **A30, prefix semantics:** with the default `https://www.bsbsb.top` (no path) the prefix is empty, so every path on that host still matches — same as before, and correct for the default. The narrowing only takes effect when a user sets a server *with* a path. I did not add a port to the reserved-host check; `https://api.bilibili.com:8443/sb` is refused on the host alone.\n- **A30, existing bad values:** a `blockServer` already saved that the new rule rejects now makes `_isBlockServer` false — SponsorBlock requests to it would carry cookies rather than none. The dialog will refuse to save it again. Arguably it should be reset to the default on load; I left it, since silently rewriting a user setting is worse.\n- **A31:** the `finish()` split relies on `extra['_rt']` being absent on the caller's own attempt and present on every nested one. That holds because `RequestOptions` is shared across retries. If some other interceptor were to copy or clear `extra`, the outermost attempt could be misclassified and the error would be rejected instead of forwarded. Not the case today.\n- **A37, residual risk:** coalescing is now safe for every parameter-changing path I found, but the guarantee is a call-site convention, not a type-level one — a future controller that mutates request state and calls `onRefresh()` directly without `markRefreshStale()` would attach to a stale refresh. The doc comment on `markRefreshStale` says so. A stricter design would thread the parameters through `queryData`, which is a much larger refactor.\n- **A37, error propagation:** a second caller that attaches now also sees the first request's error. Previously it would have issued its own request and seen its own error. Same class of failure, different instance.\n\n## TEST RESULTS\n\n```\nTEST RESULTS:\n  runner: flutter test (+ dart analyze)\n  command: dart analyze lib test && flutter test\n  exit_code: 0\n  total: 114\n  passed: 114\n  failed: 0\n  skipped: 0\n  duration_ms: ~3300 (flutter test); analyze ~40000\n\nINFRA REPAIRS (during auto-repair, empty if none):\n  (none)\n\nREAL FAILURES (audit-fix-caused regressions, empty if none):\n  (none)\n\nINFRA-PERSISTENT (failures that hit the 3-cycle repair cap, empty if none):\n  (none)\n\nOVERALL: PASS\n```\n\n`dart analyze lib test` exits 0 with the same 36 pre-existing `info` lints in vendored widget copies — unchanged, none in any file touched here. The suite is 114 tests (106 before, +8 from the three regression files I added).","ttft_ms":9207,"type":"result","duration_ms":1197269,"uuid":"95a49ae7-b6e5-4d26-9a55-44a854d5cf58","ttft_stream_ms":9049,"time_to_request_ms":755,"first_content_frame_ms":9049,"queued_turn_count":0,"result_index":0}
